FORBIDDEN-H CARRIER SPLITS
--------------------------
n=5 exact unit edges: 7 = spine 4 + tile/bulk 3; literal unit-tournament H=15.
  Reading: the H=7 obstruction is not contradicted.  The scalar 7 is
  legal here because it is an additive edge count split across carriers,
  not a single tournament H evaluation.
n=11 triangular/Harborth edges: 21 = spine 10 + lattice tile/bulk 11; exact planar u(11)=23.
  Reading: H=21 appears as a triangular-lattice lower-bound echo, while
  the exact small planar optimum has already jumped to 23.  Again the
  21 is an edge/carrier scalar, not a literal H=21 tournament.

TOURNAMENT ANALYSIS OVER CARRIER PACKETS
----------------------------------------
Vertices are carrier packets/proof obligations, not points.
Pairwise observable: which carrier better preserves traceability, the H-gap guardrail, and the exact-vs-lattice scaling channel.
Switches: geometry, H-gap, and scaling gauges; ties use insertion HP.

geometry gauge:
  score_hist={0: 1, 1: 1, 2: 1, 3: 1, 4: 1, 5: 1, 6: 1, 7: 1, 8: 1} directed_3cycles=0 SCCs=[[0], [1], [2], [3], [4], [5], [6], [7], [8]] H=1
  tie Hamiltonian path:
    score=8 unit-spine Hamiltonian path: keeps the path predicate: the unit graph is traceable
    score=7 boundary frontier shell: records the +3 gain and perimeter deficit recursion
    score=6 literal unit-tournament H: counts directed Hamiltonian paths; odd and avoids 7,21 in S599z
    score=5 equidecomposability ledger: records the scissors split behind same-cardinality counts
    score=4 tile/bulk unit-edge packet: turns u(n) into spine plus non-spine unit tiles
    score=3 Moser/non-lattice exact carrier: keeps the exact planar side beyond the triangular lattice
    score=2 round-LRC worry-set channel: imports the known round-tournament H-gap propagation channel
    score=1 OCF H-gap guardrail: blocks collapsing edge counts into forbidden tournament H values
    score=0 raw edge-count quotient: forgets whether an edge count is spine, tile, or proof side-channel

